    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Item\n",
        "<!--https://pystac.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pystac.html#pystac.Item-->\n",
        ":::{.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Check-in\n",
        "Our search returned several items. Run the code below to see what distinguishes them.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "for scene in items:\n",
        "    print(scene.id, scene.properties['datetime'], scene.properties['gsd'])\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Here `gsd` stands for [ground sample distance at the sensor](https://github.com/radiantearth/stac-spec/blob/master/commons/common-metadata.md#instrument), in meters (m). This is the pixel size of the raster. \n",
        "\n",
        "1. What differs between the items besides the year?\n",
        "2. Suppose you want to compare the vegetation around NCEAS with the 2018 image from the [`rioxarray` lesson](lesson-15-rioxarray/lesson-15-rioxarray.qmd). Which item would you pick, and why? \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--\n",
