        "-->\n",
        "\n",
        "In our search the items are listed from newest to oldest, so `items[0]` is the most recent scene.\n",
        "We'll work with this one for the rest of the lesson:"
      ],
      "id": "835c5e7d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Get first (most recent) item in the catalog search\n",
        "item = items[0]\n",
        "type(item)"
      ],
      "id": "cc75f10a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Remember the [STAC item](https://pystac.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/pystac.html#pystac.Item) is the core object in a STAC catalog. \n",
        "The item does not contain the data itself, but rather metadata and assets. The assets contain links to access the actual data.\n",
        "Some of the metadata:"
      ],
      "id": "414b2278"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Print item ID and properties\n",
        "print('ID:' , item.id)\n",
        "item.properties"
      ],
      "id": "fe48a8d0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::{.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Check-in\n",
        "From the item's properties, when was this image taken, at what resolution, and in what CRS?\n",
        "Is the time of day in `datetime` believable?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--\n",
        "Answer (2024 item): datetime 2024-06-25, gsd 0.6 m, CRS EPSG:26911 (NAD83 / UTM zone 11N).\n",
        "The time is a placeholder: all NAIP items show T00:00 or T16:00, so only the date is meaningful.\n",
        "-->\n",
        "\n",
        "### Footprint\n",
        "\n",
        "The **footprint** of the item is the area on the ground its data covers. We can access it with the `geometry` attribute:"
      ],
      "id": "fcd67bc2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "item.geometry"
      ],
      "id": "7f3122cd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Before loading the data we want to see how the item intersects with our `aoi` around NCEAS. To do this, we create a `gpd.GeoDataFrame` for each of the geometries. The new piece is the `shape()` function from the `shapely` package, which turns a GeoJSON-type dictionary into a geometry. Both our `aoi` and the item's geometry are GeoJSON-type dictionaries, and STAC geometries always use longitude and latitude coordinates (EPSG:4326)."
      ],
      "id": "44766190"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Turn the AOI and the item's footprint into geodataframes\n",
        "aoi_gdf = gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=[shape(aoi)], crs='EPSG:4326')\n",
        "footprint = gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=[shape(item.geometry)], crs='EPSG:4326')"
      ],
      "id": "fa1a75b9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The code below plots the item's footprint together with our area of interest.\n",
        "<!-- Read it before running it: most of it uses tools you already know from `geopandas`. -->\n"
      ],
      "id": "7571b5c6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Plot the footprint outline and the AOI on the same axis\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "footprint.plot(ax=ax, color='none', edgecolor='black')\n",
        "aoi_gdf.plot(ax=ax, color='red')\n",
        "ax.set_title('NAIP item footprint (black) and our area of interest (red)')\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "610469b2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Our area of interest is a small part of the item.\n",
        "When we search with `intersects`, the catalog returns every *whole* item that touches our area of interest.\n",
        "It doesn't clip the data to it.\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--\n",
        "Answer: the footprint is about 6.5 km × 7.7 km, around 85 times the area of the AOI.\n",
