      "source": [
        "![](/book/images/lesson-16/sb-from-stac-item.png){width=\"70%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exercises\n",
        "\n",
        "The [Copernicus Digital Elevation Model (DEM)](https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/group/copernicus-dem) collection contains elevation data at 90 m spatial resolution @esa_copernicus_dem_glo90. The collection ID in the MPC catalog is `'cop-dem-glo-90'`.\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose you want to know how high above sea level the area around NCEAS is, for example to start thinking about its flood or sea-level-rise risk.\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.callout-tip}\n",
        "## Part A: Access the data\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Explore the dataset's [landing page in the MPC catalog](https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/dataset/cop-dem-glo-90). Who produced this data, how was it made and what is its spatial resolution?\n",
        "2. Search the catalog for items in this collection that intersect our `aoi`. How many items did you get?\n",
        "3. Get the first item in the search and look at its properties. What is its `gsd`? What is its `datetime`?\n",
        "4. Before plotting, predict: will this item's footprint be larger or smaller than the NAIP item's? Then create a geodataframe with the DEM item's footprint and plot it together with the NAIP `footprint` and `aoi_gdf`.\n",
        "5. Open the item's `'data'` asset using `rioxarray` and save it into a variable named `dem`. Check its CRS, resolution and nodata value, and plot it.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--\n",
        "Solution\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Produced from TanDEM-X radar data (DLR and Airbus, distributed through the European Space Agency's Copernicus programme).\n",
        "   It is a digital surface model (includes buildings and vegetation), at about 90 m resolution.\n",
        "\n",
        "```python\n",
        "# 2. Search\n",
        "dem_search = catalog.search(\n",
        "    collections=['cop-dem-glo-90'],\n",
        "    intersects=aoi)\n",
        "dem_items = dem_search.item_collection()\n",
        "len(dem_items)  # 1 item\n",
        "\n",
        "# 3. Item properties\n",
        "dem_item = dem_items[0]\n",
        "dem_item.properties  # gsd: 90, datetime: 2021-04-22 (a release date, not when the radar data was acquired)\n",
        "\n",
        "# 4. Footprints: the DEM item is a 1° x 1° tile, about 92 km x 111 km\n",
        "dem_footprint = gpd.GeoDataFrame(geometry=[shape(dem_item.geometry)], crs='EPSG:4326')\n",
        "\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "dem_footprint.plot(ax=ax, color='none', edgecolor='blue')\n",
        "footprint.plot(ax=ax, color='none', edgecolor='black')\n",
        "aoi_gdf.plot(ax=ax, color='red')\n",
        "ax.set_title('DEM item (blue), NAIP item (black) and AOI (red)')\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# 5. Open and inspect\n",
        "dem = rioxr.open_rasterio(dem_item.assets['data'].href)\n",
        "print('CRS:', dem.rio.crs)                 # EPSG:4326\n",
